  "headline": "Westpac's cash-comparable net profit excluding Notable Items fell 2% to $6,972m in FY25 from $7,113m in FY24 (delta -$141m), with higher operating income and lower credit impairment charges more than offset by higher expenses. Total operating income (net operating income) rose 3% to $22,464m from $21,763m; operating performance (pre-provision profit) fell 3% to $10,548m from $10,819m. Statutory net profit was $6,916m, down 1% from $6,990m. The two differ by Notable Items (hedging items): a $56m reduction in FY25 versus a $123m reduction in FY24; these non-cash items explain the statutory-to-cash gap in each period, not the year-on-year cash movement. Net interest income rose 3% on growth in average interest-earning assets; non-interest income rose 5%; operating expenses rose 9% including a $273m Fit for Growth restructuring charge; credit impairment charges fell to $424m (5bps of average loans) from $537m (7bps).",
